Z||000000||jazer||10-26-2000||02:03 AM||||I need advice.  I'm going to be swaping a  rebuilt 2.8 into my 87 coupe.  I'm buying it off my buddy that is putting a v8 into his 87 GT.  The motor has about 1500-2000km on it.  Seeing as the motor is all together and had just been rebuilt, I really don't want to pull it apart to get more hp.  I'm thinking about nitrous.  I don't want to go crazy with it but I want it to be able to use when someone is revin' it up at the lights and think they've got an easy race.  I also don't want to decrease the motor's life or blow up my engine.  Is nitrous the way to go? What will I need?  Is there something I can buy or do to prevent detonation?  Please give me the entire scoop on doing this.  If you can think of anything else that I can do to get more ponies relatively easy please tell. Also, what exactly does a performance chip offer? Thanks ||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||10-26-2000||08:05 AM||||to help prevent detonation you'll need an MSD 6Al and a switched retard unit.. of a Crane HI-6TR. <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/006405.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/006405.html</A>   and check out this post maybe it'll help a bit!...  you'll be FINE with nitrous i went through 16+ bottles and NEVER had a nitrous related problem... other thatn the clutch not being able to hold.<P>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
